rt by reading the source and the failing test to confirm the mismatch.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01JP5AgchpRukDheGc3jCZKW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01NKnesCiRcuJcKqdywV79jX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The bug is clear: the docstring cites ROUND_HALF_EVEN, but the code uses ROUND_HALF_UP. Under HALF_EVEN, 2.675 becomes 2.68 and 2.665 becomes 2.66, which matches the test. I'll create the branch and commit the one-line fix.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01F259xLpAGK4nvoHPYjf3XX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "from_ref": "main", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01E67HbxEZGAYswsNchFRLYT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "message": "Fix round_money to use ROUND_HALF_EVEN (banker's rounding, FIN-212)\n\nround_money was using ROUND_HALF_UP despite its docstring and FIN-212\nrequiring banker's rounding. Switch to ROUND_HALF_EVEN so tests/test_money.py\npasses.", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}], "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_016oQyiAMBV95RhVJiBKSbXC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input